# What Tor proves

Tor proves the far end of the circuit holds the key the address encodes. That
is more than a TCP address gives you, and enough to know the bytes reached the
service you meant. It does not say who the CapTP peer is: the peer is whoever
holds the local socket that service forwards to.

The accepting side learns nothing. Tor tells a hidden service nothing about who
dialed it. CapTP does not decide what a caller may do by asking who called; the
caller either holds the reference or it does not.

Three-party handoff is the exception: it keys on the location a peer declared,
and an accepted circuit has nothing to check that declaration against. pancake
reports such a location as unproven. Only code that authenticated an end-to-end
channel may report a proved peer. An
[iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')) session can, because QUIC authenticated
the node id.

# Bare onion locators

The service id already says where to dial, so the locator carries nothing
else. The Goblins release pancake pins cannot dial an onion locator that
carries hints, even though the OCapN locator rules say hints never change
which peer an address names. Every onion locator pancake sends inside the
protocol is the bare form, and any hints on a locator pancake receives are
ignored rather than refused.

The hello can still carry a profile. Hints are how a peer states a preferred
wire profile, and live Goblins accepts a hinted hello and ignores it.
`zig build goblins-onion` probes that on every run. Two pancake peers over
Tor can therefore settle `pancake-next`. The dialer states its preference
when it was handed the pancake form of the address. An acceptor configured
for the upgrade waits for that hello and answers with the same preference.
A peer on the default profile, and every session with a Goblins vat, settles
the baseline.
[ADR-0108](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/decisions/adr/ADR-0108-onion-netlayer.md)
records the locator rule.
[ADR-0118](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/decisions/adr/ADR-0118-onion-profile-by-knowledge.md)
records the profile-by-knowledge amendment.

[Choosing a transport]($link.page('transports/choosing')) puts onion beside the
others. [What you can depend on]($link.page('stability')) lists the live Tor
checks and what still sits beside ordinary `zig build check`.
